From 555996a355e2cdf9bb44a59dc6b0f4146740aa1b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hectorqin <14220132+hectorqin@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 14:24:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/8] feat(agent-api): permission mode per run, capabilities
 and session status

POST /api/agent took every run with permissions bypassed. It now accepts
permissionMode, validated per provider (claude: bypassPermissions, default,
acceptEdits, plan; codex: bypassPermissions, default, acceptEdits; opencode:
bypassPermissions, default; cursor: bypassPermissions). Omitting it keeps
the old behaviour.

GET /api/agent/capabilities reports the accepted modes, and
GET /api/agent/sessions/:id reports whether a session has a run in
progress without starting one, so a caller that lost track of its runs
(e.g. after a restart) can tell a working session from a stopped one.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
